WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:08.800 align:start position:19%
The pay phone at my gas station rang at
3:33 a.m. The caller ID showed my

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:16.720 align:start position:19%
mother's number. My mother had been dead
for 11 years. So yes, I answered it.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:22.560 align:start position:19%
It was not my mother. It was a man
breathing hard, counting down from 10.

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:26.880 align:start position:19%
At one, he whispered my name. I am Jack
Doyle. Three years I worked nights at

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:32.880 align:start position:19%
mile 61.
Mile 61 sat off Interstate 40 in the New

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:37.840 align:start position:19%
Mexico desert. Your headlights were the
only lights for an hour. One pump

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:43.600 align:start position:19%
island, one ancient ice machine, and a
gray pay phone dead since 1994, bolted

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:48.160 align:start position:19%
to the brick wall. Everybody knew that
phone was dead. The company stopped

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start position:19%
paying the line years ago. Then came
October the 14th, two years ago. Dead

00:00:51.200 --> 00:01:00.079 align:start position:19%
quiet. I was restocking the cooler when
I heard it. the pay phone ringing.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.400 align:start position:19%
I went out with a flashlight. The lot
was empty. The phone rang anyway. The

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:12.400 align:start position:19%
LCD glowed faint green. The number made
my stomach drop. I knew it by heart. My

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:19.280 align:start position:19%
mother's old landline disconnected 11
years ago. I picked it up. Loneliness

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:25.280 align:start position:19%
makes you stupid at 3:33 in the morning.
5 seconds of static far away. An engine

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:30.960 align:start position:19%
idling. Then a voice began to count.
10 9 8 He was not talking to me. He was

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:38.799 align:start position:19%
reading instructions to himself.
Seven 6 5 He stopped and the static

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:46.560 align:start position:19%
stretched thin like the line was holding
its breath. Then very softly, Jack Doyle

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:53.200 align:start position:19%
locked the door and the line went dead.
I have told many scary stories here and

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:58.560 align:start position:19%
honestly this one genuinely scared me. I
owe you honesty. The jack in this story

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:03.600 align:start position:19%
is me. I worked that shift. I answered
that phone. I locked the front door and

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:07.399 align:start position:19%
sat behind the counter till sunrise, a
bat across my knees.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:15.360 align:start position:19%
At 4:47 a.m., a black pickup rolled in,
headlights off, and parked by the pay

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:20.239 align:start position:19%
phone. The driver never came in. He
stood in the dark beside the phone like

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:25.360 align:start position:19%
he was waiting for it to ring. Then he
drove off. I called my boss at dawn. He

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:30.800 align:start position:19%
laughed and said, "The desert plays
trick." But at 3:32 the next night, I

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:36.640 align:start position:19%
woke on my couch wide awake like
somebody whispered my name. At 3:33, my

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:43.599 align:start position:19%
shift started with a ringing phone. The
pay phone again. This time, no caller

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:49.360 align:start position:19%
ID. Almost did not answer. Then my hand
moved on its own. Static the engine, but

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:55.280 align:start position:19%
no counting. Pump four is leaking, he
said. Tell them at the pump, Jack.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:03:00.560 align:start position:19%
Who is this? I said. He laughed a short
wet sound and hung up. I walked to pump

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:05.360 align:start position:19%
four with the flashlight. The concrete
was dark and sticky with gasoline.

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:10.000 align:start position:19%
I shut the pump down and called the fire
department. The manager said I saved the

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:16.000 align:start position:19%
whole building. A spark near a leaking
pump could have turned mile 61 into a

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:20.959 align:start position:19%
crater. The voice had saved my life.
That is what kept me answering. The

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:25.040 align:start position:19%
voice knew things before they happened.
On the third night, the blue truck at

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:30.480 align:start position:19%
pump two do not let him use the card
reader. Take care.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:36.959 align:start position:19%
If stories like this are why you're
here, hit subscribe now. I have darker

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:42.400 align:start position:19%
ones. The blue truck pulled in at 2:10
a.m. The driver paid with a card at pump

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:46.720 align:start position:19%
2. I told him the reader was acting up
and took cash. He stared, paid, and

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:51.519 align:start position:19%
drove off cursing.
Two days later, the sheriff came about a

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:56.720 align:start position:19%
skimmer on pump 2's reader planted that
very night. Every call was like that.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:01.760 align:start position:19%
Warnings, little rescues. The voice
never asked for anything, never

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:06.640 align:start position:19%
explained. I started keeping a notebook.
Every word, every prediction, night

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:11.680 align:start position:19%
after night, night 11, the woman with
the flat tire, walk her to the pay

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:18.639 align:start position:19%
phone, stand between her and the road.
She was shaking. 22. a car following her

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:24.400 align:start position:19%
for 30 miles. I stood where he said.
Night 14. Do not drink the coffee after

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:29.919 align:start position:19%
two. The creamer has turned. Small
things, human things. I still think

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:34.800 align:start position:19%
about that detail. The creamer. Why
would a ghost care if my coffee was

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:40.639 align:start position:19%
sour? That night I started talking to
him. Who are you? I said for a long time

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:46.479 align:start position:19%
only the engine.
Then I am the man who did not lock his

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:52.400 align:start position:19%
door. The line went quiet like a held
breath. What does that mean? I asked. 30

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.360 align:start position:19%
years. I have counted down for 30 years.
Tonight I reach 1. My blood went cold.

00:04:55.759 --> 00:05:03.040 align:start position:19%
That is what he did the first night.
Whisper my name at. The register clock

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:08.320 align:start position:19%
said 3:31. 2 minutes until the phone
rang. My hand shook too badly to write.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:13.520 align:start position:19%
I flipped the notebook to the first page
and I saw it. Hi, I'm Yobi. Welcome to

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:22.479 align:start position:19%
Tales of Dread.
&gt;&gt; The handwriting on night one was not

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:27.120 align:start position:19%
mine. Neat looping letters. 10 9 8 He
does not know yet. Keep him alive until

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:32.080 align:start position:19%
he does.
I never wrote that. I swear I never saw

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:38.000 align:start position:19%
those words until that second by
flashlight. The pay phone rang at 3:33,

00:05:35.759 --> 00:05:44.000 align:start position:19%
right on time. I ran outside. The lot
was empty. No caller. I did. I picked

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:49.360 align:start position:19%
up. What happens when you reach one? The
engine was closer now, like it was

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:53.680 align:start position:19%
idling in our lot.
When I reach one, he said. He walks in.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:58.560 align:start position:19%
And this time, Jack, you will not be
behind the counter.

00:05:55.919 --> 00:06:04.479 align:start position:19%
What do you mean? I whispered. Lock the
door. Stand between her and the road.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:09.520 align:start position:19%
Somebody has to answer. I turned through
the glass. The black pickup rolled in.

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:16.880 align:start position:19%
Headlights off, parking by the pay
phone. And I understood all at once. The

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:23.199 align:start position:19%
man getting out was me, older, 30 years
older. He looked at the pay phone, then

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:30.960 align:start position:19%
at me, and mouthed three words. Do not
pick up. The voice was counting again.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:35.120 align:start position:19%
10, 9, 8. The older me shook his head,
pointing at the receiver. I dropped the

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:39.759 align:start position:19%
phone. It swung against the brick. The
counting stop midnumber like a needle

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:43.280 align:start position:19%
ripped off a record. The older me
climbed into his truck and drove into

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:48.560 align:start position:19%
the desert without a sound. The tail
lights just faded.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:54.240 align:start position:19%
When I picked the receiver up, no
engine, no voice, only the soft hiss of

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:58.160 align:start position:19%
a line dead since 1994.
I quit that morning. Told my boss the

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:03.120 align:start position:19%
desert was getting to me. People quit
mile 61 all the time. They tore the

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:07.039 align:start position:19%
station down a year later. The pay phone
went to a landfill.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:13.840 align:start position:19%
But here is what still keeps me up at
night. Nobody else will say it. Two

00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:19.759 align:start position:19%
weeks ago, at 3:32 a.m., I woke in my
own bed, wide awake, like somebody

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:26.400 align:start position:19%
whispered my name. At 3:33, my cell
phone rang, no caller ID, and faintly in

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:33.199 align:start position:19%
the background, an engine idling. I did
not answer. I sat in the dark and

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:39.199 align:start position:19%
counted along. 10 9 8 down to one. It
stopped in the silence. A whisper like

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:44.160 align:start position:19%
breath on glass. Jack Doyle, lock the
door. If that gave you chills,

00:07:41.599 --> 00:07:47.960 align:start position:19%
subscribe. The next story is the one I
have been afraid to tell.

